Here's a pricing page built around cassette/liner-note ephemera (the visual world indie podcasting actually lives in) rather than a generic SaaS pricing template — three tiers named for how a show grows, laid out like paper J-cards on a studio desk, with a monospace "tape counter" treatment for the numbers people actually compare.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Pricing — Feedline</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400..800&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
