</head>
<body>
<main class="desk">

  <header class="intro">
    <h1>Choose how your show gets heard.</h1>
    <p>Hosting for people making podcasts on their own terms — pick a plan, keep every episode, and take your feed with you if you ever leave.</p>
    <div class="billing-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Billing period">
      <button type="button" class="billing-option is-active" data-period="monthly">Monthly</button>
      <button type="button" class="billing-option" data-period="annual">Annual — 2 months free</button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="tiers">

    <article class="tier" data-tier="bedroom">
      <h2 class="tier-name">Bedroom Broadcast</h2>
      <p class="tier-line">For a first season, finding its voice.</p>
      <p class="price">
        <span class="price-amount">Free</span>
      </p>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><span class="stat">3 hrs</span> uploaded per month</li>
        <li><span class="stat">500</span> downloads per month</li>
        <li>Distribution to Spotify, Apple, YouTube &amp; more</li>
        <li>Basic embeddable player</li>
        <li>Download analytics</li>
        <li>1 show, 1 seat</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="cta" href="#">Start for free</a>
    </article>

    <article class="tier tier--featured" data-tier="onair">
      <span class="badge">On the air</span>
      <h2 class="tier-name">On Air</h2>
      <p class="tier-line">For a show that's found its audience.</p>
      <p class="price">
        <span class="price-amount" data-monthly="$16" data-annual="$13">$16</span><span class="price-period">/mo</span>
      </p>
      <ul class="features">
        <li>Unlimited uploads</li>
        <li><span class="stat">15,000</span> downloads per month included</li>
        <li>Everything in Bedroom Broadcast</li>
        <li>Auto-generated transcripts</li>
        <li>Listener tip jar</li>
        <li>IAB-certified analytics</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="cta" href="#">Go on air</a>
    </article>

    <article class="tier" data-tier="syndicate">
      <h2 class="tier-name">Syndicate</h2>
      <p class="tier-line">For a network running more than one feed.</p>
      <p class="price">
        <span class="price-amount" data-monthly="$42" data-annual="$35">$42</span><span class="price-period">/mo</span>
      </p>
      <ul class="features">
        <li>Unlimited uploads &amp; downloads</li>
        <li><span class="stat">Up to 5</span> shows on one account</li>
        <li>Everything in On Air</li>
        <li>Dynamic ad insertion &amp; marketplace access</li>
        <li>Custom domain for your show site</li>
        <li>5 team seats with role permissions</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="cta" href="#">Talk to us</a>
    </article>

  </section>

  <p class="footnote">Downloads past your plan's limit are metered at a flat rate — never cut off mid-episode. No contracts. Cancel from your dashboard any time and export your RSS feed with you.</p>

</main>

<script>
  const options = document.querySelectorAll('.billing-option');
  const amounts = document.querySelectorAll('.price-amount[data-monthly]');
  const periods = document.querySelectorAll('.price-period');

  options.forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      options.forEach(o => o.classList.remove('is-active'));
      btn.classList.add('is-active');
      const period = btn.dataset.period;
      amounts.forEach(el => {
        el.textContent = period === 'annual' ? el.dataset.annual : el.dataset.monthly;
      });
      periods.forEach(el => {
        el.textContent = period === 'annual' ? '/mo, billed yearly' : '/mo';
      });
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Design notes:** dark umber "desk" background with warm paper cards (torn top edge via `clip-path`, no rounded corners or drop shadows) stands in for the SaaS card-kit default; amber and teal split the accent duties (recommended-plan marker vs. data figures) instead of one bright accent color; the only monospace usage is on the actual usage numbers, styled like a tape counter; and the one animation is a single on-load settle with a stagger, disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

