│   ░▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚▚░       │  striped awning
│   ░  PANIFICIO ALAIMO  ░      │  plaque, centered
│   ░       dal 1962     ░      │
│   ╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╰◡╯      │  scalloped edge
│  The wood oven hasn't gone    │  left-aligned ethos line
│  cold in sixty-three years.   │
├──────────────────────────────┤
│  How it started               │  narrow prose column
│  Salvatore Alaimo lit...      │
├──────────────────────────────┤
│ 1962 ─╮                       │
│       Salvatore & Rosa...     │  sequence, squiggle connector
│ 1988 ─╯╮                      │
│        Vincenzo...            │
│ 2016 ──╯                      │
│        Ninetta...             │
├──────────────────────────────┤
│  What comes out of the oven   │
│ [Sfincione] [Cannoli]         │  asymmetric grid, folded
│    [Cassata]    [Brioche]     │  corners, varied tints
├──────────────────────────────┤
│      Via Argenteria Vecchia   │  centered chalkboard sign
│      Tue–Sun, 7–2 & 4–8       │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

**Principles:** the sign is the hero, not a stat strip — this isn't a product with metrics. Sequence markers are used once, only where the content is genuinely chronological. No card kit, no uniform shadows, no eyebrow labels, no arrows on links.

**Revised after review:** my first instinct was terracotta rooftops, cream plaster walls, and a single high-contrast serif — that's calibration trait 1 (cream background, serif display, `#D97757`-adjacent accent) wearing a Sicilian coat of paint. I replaced it with the majolica-tile and painted-cart palette (navy/cobalt/egg-yolk/olive) and swapped the serif-display headline for slab-serif signage lettering paired with a plain book serif for body text, because Caltagirone ceramics and *carretto siciliano* painting are a more specific, less-generic Sicilian reference than sunbaked terracotta, and nothing in the palette sits near `#D97757`.

