**Principles** — One bold gesture (the waveform), everything else disciplined. Tier differentiation by a single color rule, not by size, shadow, or badges. No decoration that isn't doing informational work.

**Review against the brief:** My first instinct matched the common AI defaults on two counts — I'd initially picked a cream `#F4F1EA`-adjacent background and a terracotta-family accent. I pushed the background toward a kraft/cardboard tone (justified by the tape-box subject matter) and moved the accent to a distinctly different amber hue, further from Anthropic's clay. I also dropped an initial "→" on the secondary link and ALL-CAPS tier eyebrows — neither earns its place here. Square corners and no shadows replace the default SaaS card treatment, justified by the hardware/channel-strip metaphor rather than novelty for its own sake.

