# Timberline Search & Rescue — site design

**Proposal:** A recruitment site for a volunteer mountain SAR team, invented here as *Timberline Search & Rescue*, serving the Front Range. Audience: capable, outdoorsy adults weighing a serious volunteer commitment. Primary job: explain honestly what joining costs and requires, and move a serious prospect to an info session. Building on that now.

## Design plan

**Color**
- `#EDEEE8` Snowline — paper-grey background, cooler than the typical cream
- `#1F3A2E` Spruce — primary text, dark fills
- `#4B4F4A` Granite — secondary text
- `#E8540C` Blaze — rescue-orange accent (saturated safety orange, not a clay tone)
- `#6E93A6` Glacier — cool secondary accent, used sparingly for water/ice references
- `#C9C4B4` Contour — faint line color for topo linework

**Type**
- Big Shoulders Display (600/700/900) — condensed, engineered, for the headline and large numerals. Justified by the subject: trailhead signage and USGS elevation labels are compressed for space.
- Work Sans (400/500/600) — humanist body face for legibility, field-manual plainness.

**Layout concept**
Left-aligned, asymmetric, like a map sheet rather than a marketing page — a title block in the corner, not centered hero text. The hero background is a line-drawn topographic contour pattern, not a photo or gradient.

```
+----------------------------------------------+
| TIMBERLINE SAR                                |
| ~~~~~contour lines rising behind headline~~~~ |
| We go where the                               |
| trail ends.                                   |
| [subhead, 2 lines]                            |
| [Attend an info session]  [See how to join]   |
+----------------------------------------------+
| The work — 3-item left-aligned list           |
+----------------------------------------------+
| The path to joining — 5 waypoints, dashed     |
| trail line connecting them, left-aligned      |
+----------------------------------------------+
| Requirements — spec sheet, rule-separated     |
+----------------------------------------------+
| Who joins — 2 field-notebook quotes           |
+----------------------------------------------+
| FAQ — plain Q/A                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
| Next info session / contact — sign-out board  |
+----------------------------------------------+
```

**Principles:** contour lines as the one recurring visual device (literal to the subject, not decoration); numbered steps only where content is genuinely sequential (the join process); one deliberate motion moment (contour lines draw in on load); everything else quiet — no cards, no shadows, no rounded corners.

**Revision against the default:** my first instinct was a cream background with a terracotta accent and rounded stat cards for "requirements" — I cut both. Swapped cream for a cooler grey-white, terracotta for true safety orange, and turned the requirement cards into a left-aligned spec list, which also reads more like a gear checklist than a SaaS pricing table.

## Build

