Self-critique: the contour-line hero and dashed trail path are doing the one memorable job; I kept requirements and quotes deliberately flat (no cards, no shadows) so they don't compete with it. Focus states, reduced-motion, and mobile stacking are handled. One thing I'd sanity-check in a browser: the ridge-line SVG path values are hand-tuned and should be eyeballed against the actual hero height once real content/fonts load, since condensed display type can push the headline taller than the sketch assumed.

