# Design brief

**Subject & audience:** Spindle — hosting for indie podcasters who record in a spare room, not a studio: solo hosts, two-person shows, small teams growing past their first ten episodes. **Job of the page:** get a visitor to the right tier fast and start a show — not sell them on features they don't have yet.

## Plan

**Color** — `#333B35` graphite-sage (page bg), `#262D28` deep pine (footer/dark bands), `#E7E3CE` tape-label ivory (cards), `#221D14` ink (text on ivory), `#EDE9DD` warm paper (text on dark), `#D9932E` VU-amber (primary actions), `#B23A2E` peak-red (used once, for the "peak reading" tier only).

**Type** — Fraunces (display, a soft-slab serif with real character) for headlines and the wordmark; Work Sans for everything else; Space Mono reserved for price digits and the tape counter — a mechanical-readout feel, not a generic monospace label treatment.

**Layout** — left-aligned throughout, no centered hero. Hero is two columns: headline + an actual speech waveform (irregular bar heights, not a decorative gradient). Pricing is three cards; the middle one is lifted and marked with a red tab reading "Peak pick" instead of a badge — a nod to a VU meter's peak reading rather than a generic ribbon.

```
[Spindle]                    Features  Pricing  Log in [Start]
Press record.
We'll handle the rest.        ▁▃▇▄▂▅▇▃▁▂▆▅▂▁▄▇▃▁
Spindle hosts, distributes...
[Start your show] [See plans]

Plans built for how shows actually grow
+----------+  +------------+  +----------+
| Starter  |  |Creator ▲Peak|  | Studio   |   <- middle card raised
| $00      |  | $12         |  | $29      |
| ...      |  | ...         |  | ...      |
+----------+  +------------+  +----------+

Compare in detail (hairline table)
FAQ (native <details>, left-aligned)
Footer
```

**Principles** — one bold accessory (the waveform + the peak-red tab), everything else quiet; structural marks (the red tab, the table rules) encode real meaning, not decoration; copy stays plain and active ("Start your show," never "Submit").

**Self-check against clichés** — not cream-bg+terracotta (ivory is a card color on a dark page, amber ≠ terracotta); not near-black+neon (bg is a muted sage-graphite with two distinct accents doing two different jobs); not identical SaaS cards (middle card is physically offset, sharp 3px corners not full rounding, hard flat shadow not soft grey glow); no ALL-CAPS eyebrows, no middle-dot metadata, no em-dash labels, no arrow-suffixed buttons, monospace used only where a tape counter would actually use it (prices).

## Build

