# Design plan

**Subject & angle:** A one-oven family bakery in Ortigia (the old island quarter of Syracuse, Sicily), open since 1962, now on its third generation. The page should feel like it was built around the actual shop — its oven, its tiles, its recipes — not a generic "heritage brand" template.

**Color** (5, named for what they actually are in this shop):
- `--semolina: #ECE1C3` — the flour-dusted counter, base background
- `--ink: #2B1D14` — espresso-dark crust, primary text
- `--majolica: #21586B` — Caltagirone ceramic tile blue, primary accent
- `--marsala: #8B2B2B` — Marsala wine red, secondary accent
- `--citrus: #D69A2D` — semolina/lemon gold, used sparingly (tile trim, timeline dots)
- `--pistachio: #6E7A3E` — used only as a fourth tile trim color, for rhythm

**Type:**
- Display — **Bodoni Moda** (italic weight for the wordmark and section heads). Bodoni is genuinely Italian, invented in Parma — a rooted choice rather than a generic warm serif.
- Body/UI — **Work Sans**, sentence case throughout, no tracked-out caps.
- Scale: 16px body / 1.6 line-height; headings step up 16→20→28→40→64px; body columns capped near 62ch.

**Layout concept:**
```
[nav: wordmark · story · what we bake · family · visit]

+-------------------------+----------------------+
| Forno Alaimo (italic)   |  oven-glow gradient   |
| since 1962, ortigia     |  panel (breathes once |
| one line of story copy  |  on load)             |
| Read our story          |                       |
+-------------------------+----------------------+

  1962 | Carmela opens a one-room forno...
  1978 | Turi builds the wood oven...
  2003 | Rosa and Nino take over...
 today | same oven, same starter...

[ pane di casa ][ biscotti regina ][ cassatelle ]
[ sfincione     ][ cannoli         ][ cuccidati  ]
   (hard-edged tiles, colored trim, no shadow)

  (Carmela) (Turi) (Rosa) (Nino)  — frames, left-aligned captions

+----------------- majolica-blue block ------------+
|  Come by for bread that's still warm              |
|  address / hours   ·   contact                    |
+----------------------------------------------------+
```
Left-aligned throughout (story text, captions, hours) — this is a working shop, not a poster; centered type would fight the register. The timeline is a real chronology, so numbered/dated markers are earned rather than decorative.

**Principles:**
1. The 1962–1978–2003–today timeline is literal family history, not a generic 3-step "process."
2. Tile trims (blue/wine/gold/olive) reference Caltagirone majolica directly, replacing the rounded-card-with-shadow default.
3. Bodoni Moda italic carries the whole personality of the page; body text stays quiet.
4. One motion moment only — the oven-glow panel breathes once on load, nothing else animates.
5. Copy is specific and sensory (real pastry names, real hours, a real street) — no "crafted with passion" filler.

**Self-review against defaults:** First draft instinct would've been cream background + terracotta accent + rounded cards — I swapped in a more saturated semolina-gold background, majolica blue/marsala as the accent pair instead of terracotta, and tile trims instead of rounded shadowed cards. Dropped an eyebrow label I'd drafted above "What comes out of the oven" — the heading didn't need one.

