**Design notes:** The tier hierarchy is expressed through waveform amplitude — Bedroom's mini-waveform is quiet and sparse, Network's is loud and dense — so the visual difference between plans carries real meaning instead of three identical cards. Broadcast (the plan most people should pick) is the one card with color, raised slightly, rather than wearing a generic "Most Popular" badge. Palette is a warm paper base with petrol teal and amber pulled from a mixing-board/VU-meter world, paired with Space Grotesk (display) and IBM Plex Sans (body) — no cream-and-serif, no dark-mode-plus-one-accent. The only motion is the hero waveform growing in once on load, and it's disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

