# Settings screen — Stillroom

## Grounding

A meditation app's settings screen is usually the least "meditative" part of the product — a form. The brief: make it feel like part of the same quiet room as the rest of the app, not an admin panel bolted onto it. Audience: people who already practice with the app and are here briefly, to adjust one thing and leave. Job of the screen: let them find and change one setting fast, without the screen demanding attention it hasn't earned.

## Design plan

**Color** — a dim, unlit-room palette instead of the usual cream/terracotta pairing. One accent, used only for state (on/active/focus), not decoration.

| Token | Hex | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `stone` | `#EDEFEC` | Background — pale, slightly cool, unlit |
| `ink` | `#26302B` | Primary text, dark green-grey (not pure black) |
| `moss` | `#4B5D4A` | Accent — active toggles, focus spine, selected states |
| `putty` | `#C7C2B2` | Dividers, inactive toggle tracks |
| `ember` | `#D8B979` | Focus glow / candlelight highlight, used once per interaction |
| `rust-quiet` | `#9C5B4A` | Destructive text only (desaturated, doesn't shout) |

**Type** — two families, clearly distinct roles, no bold/italic accenting mid-sentence.

- **Piazzolla** (serif) — screen title and section names. Regular/medium weight only; it's there for warmth and pacing, not drama.
- **Karla** (sans) — every row label, value, and button. Quiet, rounded terminals, reads calmly at small sizes.

Scale (roughly 1.25 ratio): title 28/34, hero line 17/26, section heading 15/22, row label 16/24, row value 15/22 at 70% ink opacity, button 16/24.

**Layout** — a single continuous column, ledger-style: label left, value/control right, hairline dividers between sections instead of cards. A thin vertical spine sits to the left of whichever row is focused or active and turns moss-colored — a structural device that tells you which row currently has your attention, not decoration.

```
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ ←  Settings                  │
│                               │
│  14-day streak                │
│  Next session at 7:00 tonight │
│ ─────────────────────────────│
│ Practice                      │
│ ┃ Session length      20 min ›│
│ ┃ Closing bell            ○—●│
│ ┃ Guiding voice           ●—○│
│ ┃ Background sound     Rain ›│
│ ─────────────────────────────│
│ Reminders                     │
│ ┃ Daily reminder          ●—○│
│ ┃ Time                7:00 AM›│
│ ┃ Days          S M T W T F S │
│ ─────────────────────────────│
│ Sound & haptics                │
│ ┃ Bell volume      ▬▬▬▬○───  │
│ ┃ Vibration on tap        ○—●│
│ ─────────────────────────────│
│ Appearance                    │
│ ┃ Screen  [Paper | Dusk | Auto]│
│ ┃ Reduce motion           ○—●│
│ ─────────────────────────────│
│ Account                        │
│ ┃ Name             Asha Rao ›│
│ ┃ Email       asha@rao.com ›│
│                               │
│           Sign out             │
│                               │
│    Delete account and data     │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

Alignment: left-aligned labels throughout, right-aligned values — a ledger, not centered cards. Changes take effect immediately (toggles, sliders, pickers apply on interaction); there's no "Save" button, because a settings screen in a meditation app shouldn't ask you to confirm you meant what you just did.

**Principles**
1. One accent color, spent only on state — never on decoration.
2. Dividers replace cards; nothing gets a shadow or a rounded box.
3. No save step — the interface trusts the action you just took.
4. Section names and row labels are sentence case, spoken plainly.

## Checking against the generic default

The version I'd produce on autopilot for "meditation app settings": cream `#F4F1EA` background, terracotta accent toggles, each section boxed in a rounded card with a soft drop shadow, `PRACTICE` / `REMINDERS` set in tracked-out capitals, a giant "14" streak number with "day streak" underneath as the hero, and a primary button reading "Save Changes →".

Changed:
- Dropped cream + terracotta for the slate/moss/ember palette — cream-and-clay is the single most common AI-generated look right now and would read as templated rather than considered.
- Dropped card-with-shadow sections for hairline dividers — the SaaS-card kit doesn't fit a screen whose job is to feel like one continuous, quiet space.
- Dropped all-caps section labels for sentence case — tracked-out capitals are chrome, not information.
- Dropped the giant-number hero for a quiet one-line status ("14-day streak / Next session at 7:00 tonight") — a huge number with a small label is the default treatment for any stat, and here it would compete with the practice itself for attention rather than support it.
- Dropped the "Save Changes →" button for autosave with no arrow — settings changes are direct actions, not form submissions, and the arrow is a tell with no function here.

