# Settings — Stillhouse

Grounding the brief: a meditation app's settings screen is not a sales page — it's a place someone visits *between* sits, often a little frazzled, to tune the thing that will help them slow down. The job of the screen is to be legible and calm in about four seconds, not impressive. I'll call the app **Stillhouse** (a place you go to sit, like a meeting house) so the copy has something real to refer to.

## Design plan

**Color**
| Token | Hex | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `paper` | `#E7E2D3` | Base surface — limestone, not cream |
| `ink` | `#2A2822` | Primary text, active toggle fill |
| `brass` | `#A9793F` | Single accent — singing-bowl metal, used sparingly |
| `moss` | `#6B7660` | Secondary text, confirmations |
| `stone-line` | `#D6CFBD` | Hairline dividers |
| `mist` | `#F5F2EA` | Row hover/press surface, barely lighter than paper |

No red anywhere, including for sign-out or destructive actions — weight and spacing signal seriousness instead of color, so nothing on a calming screen ever looks alarmed.

**Type**
- Display/headers: **Fraunces**, soft optical size, weight 400–500. Its uneven, ink-brush terminals give headers a handwritten warmth rather than a branded one — fits a journal, not a dashboard.
- UI/body: **Karla**. Rounded terminals stay legible at 14–15px for settings rows without going cold like a typical system sans.

**Layout**

Single column, 560px max width, left-aligned throughout except one deliberate break: the hero breathing motif is centered, the only asymmetry on the screen, so it reads as the one held moment before the list starts.

```
‹  Settings

         ◜   ◝
        ( ripple )      ← centered, only exception to left-align
         ◟   ◞
     You've practiced 42 days.
        Today: 8 minutes.

 Practice
 ────────────────────────────
 Session length            15 min ›
 Guiding voice                Mara ›
 Background sound             Rain ›
 Interval bell                  ○──●

 Reminders
 ────────────────────────────
 Daily reminder                 ●──○
 Time                         7:00 am ›
 Days                    S M T W T F S

 Sound & haptics
 ────────────────────────────
 Bell volume              ▬▬▬▬▬○──
 Vibrate on bell               ○──●

 Account
 ────────────────────────────
 Name and email                    ›
 Plan                        Free ›
 Download my data                  ›

                 Sign out
```

Rows, not cards — a flat list divided by hairline rules, like a printed ledger, rather than boxed app chrome with shadows.

**Principles**
1. Silence around content — whitespace does the calming, not just muted color.
2. One breath, once — the ripple plays a single settle-in pulse on load; nothing else on the page animates on its own.
3. No alarms — sign-out and any irreversible action stay ink-colored, never red; seriousness comes from spacing and confirmation copy, not hue.
4. Changes apply as you touch them — no Save button, so nothing is ever "unsaved" and anxious.
5. Sentence case everywhere — labels read like spoken language, not system output.

## Checked against the brief

I first reached for cream `#F4F1EA` + a warm terracotta accent — dropped it immediately, since that's both the generic AI-default palette and literally Anthropic's own accent color; brass reads warmer/metallic instead of clay, which also ties directly to a singing bowl rather than being an arbitrary swap. I also drafted the section headers as tracked-out uppercase eyebrows ("PRACTICE") before catching that it's exactly the template-chrome pattern to avoid — sentence case reads calmer anyway, which fits the brief better. Considered numbered steps (01/02/03) for the sections; rejected, since settings groups aren't a sequence. Also cut a "Save changes" button that I'd defaulted to — an always-live settings screen is both more honest and calmer than a can-lose-your-edits pattern.

## Code — header, hero, and Practice section

```html
<div class="settings">
  <header class="settings__header">
    <button class="back" aria-label="Back">‹</button>
    <h1>Settings</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="hero" aria-label="Practice summary">
    <div class="ripple" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p class="hero__line">You've practiced 42 days.</p>
    <p class="hero__line hero__line--quiet">Today: 8 minutes.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="group">
    <h2>Practice</h2>
    <ul class="rows">
      <li class="row row--nav">
        <span>Session length</span>
        <button class="row__value">15 min</button>
      </li>
      <li class="row row--nav">
        <span>Guiding voice</span>
        <button class="row__value">Mara</button>
      </li>
      <li class="row row--nav">
        <span>Background sound</span>
        <button class="row__value">Rain</button>
      </li>
      <li class="row">
        <span>Interval bell</span>
        <button class="toggle" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
          <span class="toggle__knob"></span>
        </button>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
```

