# Plan

Forno Scibetta: a family-run pasticceria in Noto, Sicily, open since 1962. Three generations — Turi and Concetta who lit the oven in 1962, their son Pino, and now his daughter Ida at the counter. That's the real content driving every choice below; I'm proposing the name and family details as fictional placeholder content you can swap.

**Color** (Caltagirone ceramics and Sicilian shopfronts, not bakery-cream-and-terracotta):
- `--cream` `#EDE6D2` — semolina flour, warmer/yellower than the usual grey-cream
- `--teal` `#1B3A34` — Sicilian shutter green, the dominant dark
- `--teal-deep` `#142B27` — depth/gradient shade
- `--sienna` `#B8481D` — carretto cart red-orange, used only as a small accent
- `--ochre` `#C99A2E` — durum wheat gold, for headlines on dark ground
- `--ink` `#2A211A` — espresso brown-black for body text

**Type**: Newsreader italic for display (old shop-glass gold-leaf lettering used serif italics, not script — this is accurate to the vernacular, not a cliché script logo) + Archivo for body/UI (a stamped, price-tag quality). One handwriting face, Caveat, used exactly once for the chalkboard hours — because that's genuinely how a bakery posts its hours, not decoration.

**Layout**: alternating dark/cream sections read like walking from the shopfront into the shop and back out — hero (dark, shopfront) → family timeline (cream, genuinely chronological so real years act as markers, not 01/02/03) → display case (dark, pastries glowing like a lit case at dusk) → recipe card for "how we stayed open" (cream, styled as an index card) → hours/address (dark, chalkboard). A single scalloped awning-valance shape marks each threshold into a dark section — used exactly twice, not on every boundary.

```
HERO (teal)                    CASE (teal)
┌──────────────────┐           ╭﹏﹏﹏﹏﹏╮ awning
│   Forno Scibetta  │           [icon][icon][icon]
│  bread & pastry,  │           cannolo cassat. mandorla
│  Noto, since 1962 │           [icon][icon][icon]
└──────────────────┘           brioche pane   granita

STORY (cream, left-aligned)     RECIPE (cream, index card)
1962 ─ Turi & Concetta light..  ┌ - - - - - - - - ┐
1978 ─ Pino takes the ovens..     2 kg durum wheat
1996 ─ Rosa writes it down..      1 family, all four
Today ─ Ida keeps the hours..     Sundays kept for eating
                                 └ - - - - - - - - ┘
VISIT (teal, chalkboard)
╭﹏﹏﹏﹏﹏╮ awning
Tue–Fri 7–20 · Sat–Sun 7–21 · Mon closed
Via Cavour 14, Noto
```

**Principles**: real years as the only "numbering" device; a chalk-on-slate icon set for the pastries (drawn in ochre stroke against the teal, echoing the same chalkboard used for hours) as the one place I spend visual boldness; sentence case throughout, no eyebrows, no arrows, no middots; one load-time entrance on the hero only, everything else quiet.

**Revision against the brief**: my first instinct was cream background, serif display, terracotta accent, rounded cards with soft shadows for the products — exactly the generic default. I flipped the dominant color to the shutter teal with cream as the secondary interior tone, moved sienna to a minor accent only, and replaced the product cards with case-label tags carrying a chalk-drawn icon, since a bakery counter is a specific real thing, not a grid of shadowed rectangles.

